begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k-6 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y=1 \\\\ (k-6)y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=6,$ then the second equation is $0=-8,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=6.$" 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186115832 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=0 \\\\  & -4x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\n\nII. The system has no solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent independent" 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186115832 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=0 \\\\  & -4x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent" 13194139534567 17592186045417 false] [17592186425937 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425950 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186425937 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425951 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186425937 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425952 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186425937 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186425937 1045 "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186425937 1046 #edb/ref 17592186425950 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186425937 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186425937 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048445 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186425937 1053 #uuid "080f971c-621c-5ccf-b883-b98c49745b79" 13194139534567 17592186045417 true] [17592186425938 1080 "k=1" 13194139534567 